  "info": {
    "title": "routeur.ai management API",
    "version": "1.0.0",
    "summary": "Configuration as code for routeur.ai: workspaces, projects, API keys and routing rules.",
    "description": "Configuration only — AI traffic goes to api.routeur.ai. Authenticate with an API token (`rtm_…`) minted in Settings → API tokens; it acts as the user who minted it, in their organisation, with their permissions.\n\n**Errors** share one envelope (`Error`): branch on `code` (a valid token whose owner lacks MFA in an organisation that requires it gets 403 `mfa_required`; any `{organisation}` slug other than the token’s, existing or not, gets 403 `org_mismatch` — a 404 always means the workspace or resource itself is missing).\n\n**Lists** are cursor-paginated: `?limit=` (1–200, default 100) and `?cursor=` from `meta.next_cursor`.\n\n**Request bodies** are strict: an unknown top-level key is a 422. PATCH: absent = unchanged, `null` clears a nullable field.\n\n**Strings are stored verbatim** — never trimmed, and `\"\"` never becomes null. Names, labels, keys and list items must not start or end with whitespace (422). A blank string (`\"\"` or whitespace only) is a 422 everywhere except free-text descriptions, where `\"\"` is stored and returned as `\"\"`. Regex patterns keep any whitespace you send.\n\n**Immutable fields.** Read-only response fields (`id`, `workspace_id`, timestamps, `state`, …) and create-only fields (marked `x-create-only: true`: workspace and project `slug`, credential `provider`) may be echoed back on update only with their current value — compared with what GET returns, timestamps as the same string. A different value is a 422 `immutable_field`; on create, read-only fields must be absent or null. Changing a create-only field means replacing the resource.\n\n**Slugs** are lowercase letters, digits and hyphens (workspaces, projects) or lowercase letters, digits and underscores (policies and rules). **`{workspace}`** in a path takes the slug or the `ws_…` id.\n\n**`enabled`** is boolean only (`null` is a 422): absent = true on create, unchanged on update or replace.\n\n**Plan features** gate create and update only; list, read and delete keep working after a downgrade, so `terraform plan` and `destroy` still succeed.\n\n**Rate limits**: per token 600 reads (GET) and 120 writes per minute; 1200 requests per minute per IP. Over the limit: 429 `rate_limited` with `Retry-After`.\n\n**Propagation**: writes reach the gateway asynchronously, usually within seconds. A 2xx means the change is stored, not that it is live; expect seconds, at worst minutes. Rotating an API key mints a new key with a new `id`.\n\n**Versioning**: within v1 changes are additive only — new endpoints, optional request fields, response fields, enum values and error codes. Clients must ignore unknown response fields and tolerate unknown enum values and codes. Breaking changes ship as /api/v2 with an overlap period. Deprecated fields and endpoints keep working, are marked `deprecated: true` here, and respond with `Deprecation` (RFC 9745) and `Sunset` (RFC 8594) headers."
  },
